<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Clinton NATO nod shows Czech stability-Prague govt.</title>
<headline>Clinton NATO nod shows Czech stability-Prague govt.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Prague government called U.S. President Bill Clinton's decision on Thursday to choose the Czech Republic as one of three preferred candidates for NATO expansion a clear sign of the country's stability.</p>
<p>&quot;The government of the Czech Republic welcomes today's announcement by President Clinton... as an evaluation of the stable development of our country until now,&quot; said a statment released by Prime Minister Vaclav Klaus's spokesman Ivo Strejcek.</p>
</text>
